xjq: no trailing newline after the last text result (checkpoint 1)

Sentence: "then join results with each on a newline". Registry T7/T45 read a result that
normalizes to the empty string as still occupying its line, so a lone empty result printed
"\n"; the hidden tests want "" and the reference solution writes "\n".join(results).
Tests: test_text_all_on_whitespace_only_element_is_empty_output (checkpoint 2),
test_json_empty_string_preserves_element_with_empty_text (checkpoint 3).

--- a/xjq/checkpoint_1.md
+++ b/xjq/checkpoint_1.md
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 ## Output
 
-- Text/attribute results: strip each result, collapse internal whitespace runs to single spaces, then join results with each on a newline.
+- Text/attribute results: strip each result, collapse internal whitespace runs to single spaces, then join results with each on a newline. No trailing newline.
 - XML node results: pretty-print serialized XML; when multiple XML nodes match, output only the first node.
 - No-match output: write nothing to stdout/stderr.
 
